{
  "info": {
    "name": "GearUp Backend API",
    "description": "Auto-generated from https://github.com/monjurulahamed/GearUp-Backend (main branch).\n\nBase path for every route is `/api` (mounted in src/app/app.ts). Auth uses a JWT sent as `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (see src/app/middlewares/checkAuth.ts) \u2014 there is no cookie-based auth despite cookie-parser being installed.\n\nHow to use:\n1. Set `baseUrl` collection variable (default http://localhost:5000/api \u2014 change the port to match your PORT env var).\n2. Run 'Auth > Register User' and 'Auth > Register Provider' once (or 'Login' if accounts exist). This auto-fills accessToken / customerToken / providerToken / userId collection variables via a test script.\n3. For ADMIN endpoints, log in with your seeded SUPER_ADMIN_EMAIL / SUPER_ADMIN_PASSWORD via 'Auth > Login', which will populate adminToken automatically.\n4. Run 'Categories > Create Category' and 'Gear > Create My Gear' to populate categoryId / gearId used by later requests.\n\nNote: the Admin folder is fully coded in the repo (admin.controller.ts / admin.route.ts) but is NOT wired into src/router/index.ts, so it currently 404s \u2014 see that folder's description.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
